Z||000001||DXR_DAD||06-16-2000||11:04 AM||||THANKS MONKEY!!!<P><BR>This is easy, the only trick to it is <BR>finding long enough screws to mount the<BR>lights, (2) on each light just like<BR>some front turn signals on many cars<P>I had to use extentions = a 2 1/2"L<BR>hex with a screw on one end and a threaded<BR>hole on the other end, I think it was<BR>8-32.  You need this much to mount because<BR>the steel/frame in about 2" in (deep) from<BR>the facsia!<P>It looks like many cars have the lights that would work I don't remember the name brand of the lights off hand I got them from Grand Auto.<P><BR>I hope this helps.<P>DXR_DAD<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 06-16-2000).]||||reg||11
Z||000002||87ECO5||06-16-2000||12:31 PM||||Those look good!<P>Monkey, after doing this mod, you could take it one step further and mist them to match the body color (like your tail lights).||||reg||14
